{"id": "EUVD-2026-67435", "enisaUuid": "3392761b-7501-30f2-bd95-d89599807442", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/vmwgfx: validate external BO copy bounds for both stride paths\n\nvmw_external_bo_copy() trusts caller-supplied offsets, strides, and\nheights and operates on imported dma-buf vmaps:\n\n  - The equal-stride memcpy() bound was clamped after subtracting the\n    offsets from dst_size and src_size; an offset larger than the BO\n    size wraps the unsigned subtraction to a huge value and the\n    resulting memcpy() runs off the end of the vmap.  dst_stride *\n    height is also a u32 multiplication that can overflow.\n  - The non-equal-stride row-by-row path had no bound at all.  The\n    loop touches bytes through offset + (height - 1) * stride +\n    width_in_bytes, with only a WARN_ON(dst_stride < width_in_bytes),\n    and could likewise step past the end of either mapping.\n\nThe offsets and strides are derived from STDU/SOU plane state, so a\nconfigured CRTC submitting a crafted atomic commit on an imported\nframebuffer can reach this path.\n\nValidate the exact row-copy endpoint against each BO's size up front\nusing check_mul_overflow() and check_add_overflow().  Use the bulk\nmemcpy() path only when width_in_bytes covers the whole stride;\notherwise copy one row at a time so partial-row updates near the bottom\nof a framebuffer remain valid.  Also reject zero strides and stride <\nwidth_in_bytes, both of which the row-by-row path cannot represent\nsafely.", "datePublished": "2026-08-28T06:53:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:26:33", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4e0f669e2951b742239c6fe847fcc406fe78748d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e7b25a6011781ebfdbc458552cae6d4156732771", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/042ca38779554687fc32b66a28328e0d9a36c58f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5e4a2d15637a906cbd9bc98e0bf969f5f713e344", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/706c93c5813caabbb0d0a576c017d15aeec2c113"], "aliases": ["GHSA-c29c-h3vq-mr67", "CVE-2026-80700"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0b0ddf44-6b8a-34eb-acf3-9ebe6857787c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9a9716bbbf3dd6b6cbefba3abcc89af8b72631f4 <4e0f669e2951b742239c6fe847fcc406fe78748d"}, {"id": "0e8daf14-0834-3eb8-a357-687eb6f6adef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "119e97c8-85c4-34cc-b615-12481e9d07a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.8"}, {"id": "18ff3765-0d1a-3fed-b139-84d761a75493", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.44"}, {"id": "5f619fa2-3903-364b-9bf8-4f23c4de1359", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "50f1199250912568606b3778dc56646c10cb7b04 <5e4a2d15637a906cbd9bc98e0bf969f5f713e344"}, {"id": "7eed7e46-ec8a-3aeb-8f51-9bd78287766a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "8cb0c20d-b467-3191-a45b-4f7417b8e214", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.10.8 <6.11"}, {"id": "8e6735b0-826f-3042-8f88-3fe00df0017c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "50f1199250912568606b3778dc56646c10cb7b04 <706c93c5813caabbb0d0a576c017d15aeec2c113"}, {"id": "9fc9a0a2-3cda-3fb3-92ff-fcb895ce7e5b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.11"}, {"id": "a30918b2-eae9-35a4-953f-3c7df4676457", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "50f1199250912568606b3778dc56646c10cb7b04 <042ca38779554687fc32b66a28328e0d9a36c58f"}, {"id": "a50d2aaf-866f-39ba-90ae-d6cbc93acef8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5c12391ee1ab59cb2f3be3f1f5e6d0fc0c2dc854"}, {"id": "ac0f1258-cecd-3cdd-8de5-e37823d1dbc8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.103"}, {"id": "b3b749f7-48e5-3fe8-8b9f-82b48c11e97e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.151"}, {"id": "c57480bd-2b24-3571-933c-9de00c3b68b2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.49 <6.6.151"}, {"id": "f8bba4dc-8039-3e0c-823e-15260189fed5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "50f1199250912568606b3778dc56646c10cb7b04 <e7b25a6011781ebfdbc458552cae6d4156732771"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "37d894ce-3d88-33d6-8d71-5f077e1cb20b", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}